efs":["DUTT-4-47-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4046006","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d648480915966e660aface040d6750a58834fef987d9721560f7dde2a76785ea","compact":"f2aeca5be7f1d688cbf11b53a8273c3d7752462db6682860cbd0b9b0d140a36d","nasal":"f2aeca5be7f1d688cbf11b53a8273c3d7752462db6682860cbd0b9b0d140a36d"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-46-7","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":46,"verse":7,"english":"And having explored the Eastern regions, as directed, the exceedingly strong Vinata not having been able to see Sītā, came back, in company with his counsellors.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-47-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4046007","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a9bfedce3a9ba8214bf46af1a7a4d9d58b06d749830383448ae563fc31ff5932","compact":"65e43aaf09eef86c3c22ca1aa5c34c229985af713d53f6e5bc293dde38ec7402","nasal":"65e43aaf09eef86c3c22ca1aa5c34c229985af713d53f6e5bc293dde38ec7402"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-46-8","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":46,"verse":8,"english":"And then that mighty ape, Satavali, daunted in spirits, arrived with his forces, after having searched all through the North.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.407,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-47-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4046008","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d08152b1a09fca8f2d51065ba2ba07d81040d5d347dedb5e75101724ade52b3b","compact":"7c4c435df70ae2619b870a8455d2d0744dc670cc7d3d958f04d622924d93316c","nasal":"7c4c435df70ae2619b870a8455d2d0744dc670cc7d3d958f04d622924d93316c"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-46-9","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":46,"verse":9,"english":"And having searched the West in company with his monkeys, Sușeņa, on the month being complete, presented himself before Sugrīva.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.583,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-47-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4046009","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"00b20e5189bc7aa0d4a23dbaccb2eff403f41c9f35690b8e723ebfdedecc5da1","compact":"23531a7e611dee81c967607914baf4aff9e69f4cf6294e803a07e5cdec9f74ca","nasal":"23531a7e611dee81c967607914baf4aff9e69f4cf6294e803a07e5cdec9f74ca"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-46-10","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":46,"verse":10,"english":"And coming to Sugrīva seated along with Rāma behind the Fountain, and saluting the former, Susena said to Sugriva.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-47-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4046010","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"286469ed8f14729745409409b4de9a71009fa49e8d0aaee07198ff115d1fcc2a","compact":"dc48c697de16b7d099d69bbbae297fed772fd7333a6ed10e18d1b5b91338a79f","nasal":"dc48c697de16b7d099d69bbbae297fed772fd7333a6ed10e18d1b5b91338a79f"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-46-11","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":46,"verse":11,"english":"Searched have been all the mountains, and deep woods, and streams, and islands embosomed in the ocean, and the various provinces. And also searched have been all the caves which have been described by you; and searched have been all the groves entertwined with plants; and thickets; and difficult and uneven grounds. And huge animals have been sought out and slain (by us). And all the impracticable places we have explored again and again.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.712,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-47-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4046011","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fin